<title>CANADA: Vancouver exchange sues Thomson unit, CBC.</title>
<headline>Vancouver exchange sues Thomson unit, CBC.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Vancouver Stock Exchange said on Friday that it was suing a Thomson Corp unit and the government-owned Canadian Broadcasting Corp for defamation.</p>
<p>Both actions were filed in the Supreme Court of British Columbia.</p>
<p>The first suit named Thomson Canada, publisher of Toronto's Globe and Mail newspaper, for an article by Margaret Cannon entitled &quot;Death on the VSE: The mysterious trail of murder and mayhem at the Vancouver Stock Exchange&quot;, published in the May Globe and Mail Report on Business magazine.</p>
<p>The second action was against the CBC and others over an interview of Cannon broadcast on the company's Vancouver radio station in April.</p>
<p>Officials at Thomson and the CBC could not be reached for comment.</p>
<p>((Reuters Vancouver Bureau (604) 664-7314))</p>
